    {
      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "sound",
      "title": "The same mark, a different tone",
      "text": "ที่, ค่ะ and ด้วย all sound falling, but not for the same reason, and ก่อน, ป่า and จ่าย are low although they carry the same ่ mark. The mark does not choose the tone alone: the class of the first letter decides what it gives. ่ on a low-class letter (ที่, ค่ะ) is falling; ่ on a mid-class letter (ก่อน, ป่า) is low; ้ on a mid-class letter (ด้วย, บ้าน) is falling. You met the table in the sound steps; here, read the line and listen to whether you hear it.",
      "explains": [
        "th.practice.tone-marks"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    }
  ],
